## 3. Pipeline architecture — what each script does

The project was developed in notebooks first (NB01–NB10), then proven code was migrated into the `ct_tfpnp` package with CLI-driven scripts. This mirrors LION's own structure: notebooks for exploration, package for production.

### Training pipeline

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  scripts/train_tfpnp.py                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
   Reads CLI args (n_train, n_epochs, σ/µ ranges,
                   reward type, π₂ warmup, etc.)
                            │
                            ▼
   Constructs:
     • Geometry        (ParallelBeam, 30 views, 512×512)
     • DRUNet          (pretrained weights loaded, frozen)
     • Policy network  (ResNet-18 + 3 heads, random init)
     • Critic network  (random init)
     • ADMM environment
     • TFPnPSolver     (inherits from LIONsolver)
                            │
                            ▼
   Loads from LION:
     • train split (3300 images, subsets to N_train)
     • val split   (401 images,  subsets to N_val)
                            │
                            ▼
   For each epoch:
     ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
     │ For each training image:                         │
     │   Run TFPnP episode (m·N = 30 ADMM steps)        │
     │   Push transitions to replay buffer              │
     │   Sample minibatch → update policy + critic      │
     │ Validate on val set (TFPnP @ 5% noise)           │
     │ Save checkpoint if val PSNR improved (★)         │
     └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
   Writes to results/learned/{exp}/:
     • checkpoint_best_val.pth   ← the result
     • tfpnp_check_*.pt          (periodic snapshots)
     • metrics_history.json      (per-step + per-epoch metrics)
     • tfpnp_final.pt
```

